WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.240
All right.

00:04.240 --> 00:08.400
So now I'm going to talk about how to use the subquery in the Select clause.

00:08.480 --> 00:14.440
So now we typically use the subqueries in the Select clause to aggregate the data side by side with

00:14.480 --> 00:16.400
the columns of the main query.

00:16.440 --> 00:16.640
Okay.

00:16.680 --> 00:20.280
So let's check the syntax of the subquery in the Select clause.

00:20.320 --> 00:25.840
So we start with the simple stuff where we say okay let's go and select a column that you want to retrieve

00:26.040 --> 00:27.440
from a specific table.

00:27.440 --> 00:28.240
So nothing new.

00:28.280 --> 00:29.880
We are just querying a table.

00:29.920 --> 00:35.480
And now what we can do in SQL is that not only we can go and select the columns from a specific table,

00:35.760 --> 00:43.120
we can go and insert here inside the select another query like a full query like select from and where.

00:43.120 --> 00:45.680
So again it's like query inside another query.

00:45.920 --> 00:48.080
And we call this of course a subquery.

00:48.080 --> 00:52.960
In order to tell SQL this is a subquery we go and add the parentheses.

00:52.960 --> 00:54.760
So with that SQL can understand huh.

00:54.800 --> 00:56.080
This is a subquery.

00:56.080 --> 00:59.520
And the result of this query is going to be used in the select.

00:59.520 --> 01:01.870
So we can handle it like any other column.

01:01.870 --> 01:03.670
We can go and give it like an alias.

01:03.710 --> 01:06.430
It is here optional and not masked to add an alias.

01:06.430 --> 01:08.990
So this inner query, we call it a subquery.

01:08.990 --> 01:11.470
And the outer query is going to be the main query.

01:11.470 --> 01:14.990
So this is how you put a subquery in the Select clause.

01:14.990 --> 01:21.950
But there is one rule for this query that the result of this subquery must be scalar query.

01:21.950 --> 01:26.470
That means the result must be a single value because otherwise it will not work.

01:26.550 --> 01:29.750
SQL here is expecting only one value.

01:29.750 --> 01:32.950
So this is how we use the subquery inside the Select clause.

01:32.990 --> 01:34.310
All right let's have the following task.

01:34.350 --> 01:40.630
And it says show the product IDs product names prices and the total number of orders.

01:40.630 --> 01:43.030
So now if we check the task there is like two parts.

01:43.030 --> 01:47.830
The first part is that we are showing the details about the products, and the second part that we have

01:47.830 --> 01:50.750
to go and calculate the total number of orders.

01:50.750 --> 01:51.870
So let's see what we're going to do.

01:51.910 --> 01:57.990
First, let's go and solve this simple part here where we have the product ID, product names and prices.

01:57.990 --> 02:05.970
So we're going to go and select the product ID and the product and then the price from the table.

02:06.450 --> 02:07.130
Sales.

02:07.130 --> 02:07.890
Products.

02:07.930 --> 02:09.370
Let's go and execute it.

02:09.410 --> 02:12.330
So with that, we have solved the first part of the task.

02:12.330 --> 02:14.530
We have the details about the products.

02:14.610 --> 02:16.450
Now we go and solve the second part.

02:16.490 --> 02:19.290
We have to go and calculate the total number of orders.

02:19.330 --> 02:22.650
Now this information come from different tables from the products.

02:22.650 --> 02:24.250
We cannot calculate it from products.

02:24.250 --> 02:26.170
We have to go and query the orders.

02:26.210 --> 02:31.690
So now what I'm going to do I'm going to go and calculate this part in separate query instead of having

02:31.690 --> 02:33.250
it here inside the products.

02:33.410 --> 02:37.690
So let's have a semicolon in order to have a second query.

02:37.850 --> 02:40.690
So we're going to go and select the total number of orders.

02:40.690 --> 02:47.010
That means we can go simply do a count star from the table sales orders.

02:47.050 --> 02:49.130
Let me just make it a little bit bigger.

02:49.130 --> 02:54.210
So we're going to call it total orders and a semicolon as well.

02:54.330 --> 02:58.770
So now if we just execute the whole thing you will get here like two parts in the results.

02:58.770 --> 03:01.480
First you have the details of the product.

03:01.480 --> 03:04.800
And the second part we have now the total number of orders.

03:04.800 --> 03:06.040
We have ten orders.

03:06.040 --> 03:11.160
But now with that we have like two different queries like separated from each other and we have two

03:11.160 --> 03:12.240
different results.

03:12.480 --> 03:16.440
But in the task we have to show all those informations in one result.

03:16.440 --> 03:20.360
So now what we can do, we can put one query inside another query.

03:20.360 --> 03:25.280
So now if you check the second query the total orders, you can see we have only single value.

03:25.280 --> 03:28.400
So we have a scalar query scalar subquery.

03:28.640 --> 03:34.080
That's why we can go with this as a subquery like this.

03:34.080 --> 03:38.040
And I'm going to go and put everything in one line in order to see it.

03:38.040 --> 03:39.720
So let's remove the semicolons.

03:39.720 --> 03:40.600
We don't need it.

03:40.600 --> 03:46.440
And now what we're going to do we're going to go and take the whole thing and put it inside the main

03:46.440 --> 03:47.080
query.

03:47.440 --> 03:50.480
So this is the main query.

03:50.480 --> 03:53.240
And now think about it as new column.

03:53.240 --> 03:55.360
So I will put the query here.

03:55.360 --> 03:58.280
So it is just one new column in our select.

03:58.280 --> 04:04.260
But in order to have it as a subquery we have to use the parenthesis at the start and at the end.

04:04.300 --> 04:06.420
And of course we have to go and give it a name.

04:06.420 --> 04:08.900
So I'm going to go and use the same name over here.

04:09.260 --> 04:12.620
So it's going to be as total orders.

04:12.620 --> 04:15.460
So that's the setup for the subquery is ready.

04:15.460 --> 04:20.180
And it is inside the Select clause in the main query.

04:20.220 --> 04:21.580
Let's go and execute it.

04:21.620 --> 04:23.820
Now as you can see we have everything together.

04:23.820 --> 04:26.540
We have the three informations the product details.

04:26.540 --> 04:29.260
And as well side by side with the total orders.

04:29.260 --> 04:33.620
And since it is always the same value it can go and be repeated for each row.

04:33.620 --> 04:38.580
So this is what we call scalar subquery inside the Select clause.

04:38.580 --> 04:40.500
And here again very important to understand.

04:40.540 --> 04:47.300
If you are using a subquery inside the Select clause only the scalar subquery is allowed.

04:47.300 --> 04:52.740
So for example instead of having one value from the aggregation we can go and use the order id.

04:53.380 --> 04:55.180
So let's see what can happen.

04:55.180 --> 04:56.260
We will get an error.

04:56.300 --> 04:59.700
It's going to say subquery is returning more than one value.

04:59.700 --> 05:04.130
And this is not allowed because we are using the subquery in the Select clause.

05:04.130 --> 05:07.290
So that's why we have to have only one value.

05:07.290 --> 05:09.570
And by using the aggregation you will get one value.

05:09.570 --> 05:12.050
So let's repair it and it's working.

05:12.090 --> 05:16.850
And now again if you would like only to see the results from the subquery what you can do you can go

05:16.850 --> 05:21.410
and highlight the subquery like this without the parenthesis of course.

05:21.450 --> 05:23.090
And you go and execute it.

05:23.090 --> 05:27.850
And with that you can see in the output that then this is the intermediate results that's going to be

05:27.850 --> 05:29.770
passed to the main query.

05:29.810 --> 05:34.290
And if you want the whole thing to be executed just like unmark it and execute.

05:34.290 --> 05:37.610
And with that everything can be executed the subquery and the main query.

05:37.610 --> 05:41.250
So this is the scalar subquery in the Select clause okay.

05:41.290 --> 05:44.970
So now let's see quickly how SQL executed this query step by step.

05:44.970 --> 05:46.570
So this is our original query.

05:46.570 --> 05:49.090
And we need two tables from our database for it.

05:49.090 --> 05:52.810
So the first step is that is going to go and identify the subquery.

05:53.050 --> 05:54.970
And it's going to go and execute it.

05:54.970 --> 05:56.650
So this is the first step.

05:56.650 --> 05:59.090
So the query is targeting the orders table.

05:59.090 --> 06:01.530
And we are just simply doing a count.

06:01.530 --> 06:01.550
Account.

06:01.550 --> 06:06.990
So in the output we will get an intermediate result where we are counting the number of rows of the

06:06.990 --> 06:07.510
orders.

06:07.550 --> 06:12.590
Now the next step that is going to go and pass this value to the main query.

06:12.590 --> 06:14.030
So this is the second step.

06:14.030 --> 06:18.230
And if you go and pass this value to the main query it's going to look like this.

06:18.230 --> 06:21.550
So you are saying product ID products and the ten.

06:21.550 --> 06:25.870
So after SQL prepared the main query SQL can go and execute it.

06:25.870 --> 06:28.030
So this time we are targeting the products.

06:28.030 --> 06:32.110
And in the output we will get all the information from the products without any filter.

06:32.110 --> 06:33.910
Because here we don't have any Where clause.

06:34.110 --> 06:35.750
And the final results.

06:35.750 --> 06:36.910
We will get it like this.

06:36.910 --> 06:41.750
So we will have the product ID, the product and the total that we got it from the subquery.

06:41.750 --> 06:47.310
So as you can see the subquery here is a scalar subquery where we have only one single value.

06:47.310 --> 06:51.350
So again it's very simple always SQL starts with a subquery.

06:51.350 --> 06:54.950
And then it's going to go and pass the values to the main query.

06:54.950 --> 06:57.590
And at the end the main query is going to be executed.

06:57.710 --> 06:59.710
And we will get the final result from it.

06:59.710 --> 07:02.670
So this is how SQL executed our query.
